claim.claim-text:
wherein the sensor device is further configured for determining said second signal as a polynomial expression of said at least two magnetic field gradients, the polynomial expression having an order of at least two;
or wherein the sensor device is further configured for determining said second signal as a polynomial expression of said at least two differences, the polynomial expression having an order of at least two;
or wherein the sensor device is further configured for determining said second signal as a sum of squares of said at least two magnetic field gradients;
or wherein the sensor device is further configured for determining said second signal as a sum of squares of said at least two differences;
or wherein the sensor device is further configured for determining said second signal as a sum of absolute values of said at least two magnetic field gradients;
or wherein the sensor device is further configured for determining said second signal as a sum of absolute values of said at least two differences.

wherein the sensor device comprises four magnetic sensitive elements;
wherein the sensor device comprises a semiconductor substrate;
wherein the sensor device is configured for measuring two first magnetic field components (Bx) oriented in a first direction (X) parallel to the semiconductor substrate, and two second magnetic field components (Bz) oriented in a second direction (Z) perpendicular to the first direction (X);
wherein the sensor device is configured for determining a first magnetic field gradient (dBx/dx) of the first magnetic field component (Bx) along said first direction (X), and for determining a second magnetic field gradient (dBz/dx) of the second magnetic field component (Bz) along said first direction (X);
wherein the sensor device is configured for determining an linear position in the first direction (X);
and wherein the sensor device is configured for calculating the second signal as a function of this first and second magnetic field gradient.

a) measuring (1201) at least four magnetic field values of said magnetic field including two first magnetic field components (Bx1, Bx2) oriented in a first direction (X), and two second magnetic field components (By1, By2; Bz1, Bz2) oriented in a second direction (Y; Z) perpendicular to the first direction at each of two sensor locations (X1, X2) spaced apart along the first direction (X);
b) determining (1202) at least two magnetic field gradients (dBx/dx, dBy/dx; dBx/dx, dBz/dx), or at least two magnetic field differences (ΔBx, ΔBy; ΔBx, ΔBz) based on said at least four magnetic field values;
c) deriving (1203) from said at least two magnetic field gradients or from said at least two magnetic field differences a first signal (POS) indicative of a position of the sensor device;
d) deriving (1204) from said at least two magnetic field gradients (dBx/dx, dBy/dx; dBx/dx, dBz/dx) or from said at least two magnetic field differences (ΔBx, ΔBy; ΔBx, ΔBz) a second signal indicative of a fault
e) providing the second signal or a signal derived therefrom.
